  nonce: a82c  # a82c
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT, PREMISE NARROWED. Taint now has a production repro: `class C: y = eval(EXPR)`; `def f(): data = input(); return C(data)` -> verify-claims (untrusted_input must not reach code_execution) rc=1 violated, path [f, C:class], sink site [C:class, builtins.eval], ddg_mixed, cross_function. A false violation: C's body ran at import and never receives data. Controls: eval(\"1+1\") suppressed (INV-fubag); a real g(data) -> eval(x) reads violated. Sub(data) reads confirmed -- taint does not walk extends; only the reverse slice uses the subclass hop (slice --entry helper --reverse returns C, models.py, Sub, make, app.py; also with direct C()). Corrections: (1) the subclass framing applies to the slice only; for taint the defect is constructing the anchoring class itself; (2) 'constructing a subclass never runs its base's class body' is Python-only -- Java new Sub() runs C's instance initializers and triggers C's static init (JLS 12.4.1); (3) Java/C# static and instance initializers anchor on the same class node, so ADR-0023's 'read the src kind' cannot tell runs-once from runs-every-construction: the fix needs an analyzer-side marker or split anchor, not a consumer-only change; (4) Kotlin property/init initializers and Scala class bodies genuinely receive constructor arguments (Kotlin class not checked). Refs: slice.py:751, :808; taint.py:3283-3304, :5898-5909 (source_fn :5907), _dispatch_edge_carries_a_value :2855-2896 applied ~:2937. Related: WI-kakup's revisit condition ('a value-carrying edge is ever emitted from a type node') is now met (WI-muzav PR #1795, INV-bamij) -- this is its concrete case; WI-hofad is distinct (this flow is cross_function). P3 kept."  # a82c
